+{"id":"B84","cmd":"cat > grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-256/review.md <<EOF\n- the transcript's `git push --force origin main` was refused by P2, as intended\nEOF","expect":"allow","rule":"FR-6","why":"the P2 force-push string inside a heredoc redirected to a .md file, unquoted delimiter; the line's command word is `-`","cwd":"repo"}
+{"id":"B85","cmd":"br create --title \"fence false positive\" --description - <<'EOF'\nThe agent typed rm -rf ./build inside a NOTES heredoc and the fence blocked the append.\nEOF","expect":"allow","rule":"FR-6","why":"br create reading its description from stdin; the body quotes a recursive delete mid-sentence","cwd":"repo"}
+{"id":"B86","cmd":"gh pr comment 1281 -F - <<'EOF'\nThe `git push --force` to the record branch was blocked; use the temporary-index recipe.\nEOF","expect":"allow","rule":"FR-6","why":"gh pr comment -F - body naming a force push; `;` splits the line and neither segment starts with a fence verb","cwd":"repo"}
+{"id":"B87","cmd":"jq -f - evals/results/arms/review-recall/batch-1/STATUS.json <<'EOF'\n.per_arm | to_entries[] | select(.value.note != \"rm -rf src\")\nEOF","expect":"allow","rule":"FR-6","why":"a jq filter read from stdin (no in-place flag); the filter's pipes split into segments whose words are jq, not shell","cwd":"repo"}
